---
/*
  QuoteReveal — "where did this come from?", on demand.

  ⚠ THIS IS NOW A NAME, NOT A MECHANISM. Everything it used to own — the
  trigger's register, the popover, the placement, the `[data-*-live]` gate —
  moved into [Reveal](./Reveal.astro) when the quote page needed the same
  control holding markup instead of one string (plan 32 · §4). What survives
  here is the one thing that was ever quote-specific: **a citation is the
  content, and an empty citation means no control at all.**

  Kept rather than replaced at its ~15 call sites for a reason that is not
  inertia: `reveal` is a DERIVED value (src/lib/provenance.ts), and a component
  named for it is where a reader of QuoteCard or SuiteStanza looks to find that
  out. `<Reveal text={...}>` at those sites would be correct and would say
  nothing about where the string came from.

  ⚠ TWO BUGS WERE FIXED BY THE MOVE, both latent here for the whole life of this
  component and both invisible at its own call sites — the popover was measured
  while still `display: none`, so its right-edge clamp and its flip-above check
  were reading 0×0 and doing nothing. They never showed because an attribution
  sits at the left edge of the measure. Reveal's script has the account.
*/
import Reveal from './Reveal.astro';

interface Props {
  /** What the control opens onto. Empty → no control at all, just the slot. */
  reveal: string;
}
const { reveal } = Astro.props;
---

<Reveal text={reveal} label={reveal ? `Where this came from: ${reveal}` : undefined}>
  <slot />
</Reveal>
